<title>FRANCE: BIS Q1 turnover increases nine pct.</title>
<headline>BIS Q1 turnover increases nine pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>French temporary work agency BIS said on Monday its first-quarter 1997 turnover rose to 1.99 billion francs from 1.83 billion francs for the same year-earlier period, an increase of nine percent on a like for like basis.</p>
<p>BIS, 93.6 percent owned by Dutch Vendex, said 10 percent of sales came from the temporary worker sector.</p>
<p>The turnover increase was six percent taking into account the July 1996 closing of the security division, BIS said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
